    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Stages of the Works Programme & Pink Book (IRFC Vol. I Chapter VI)\nThe annual planning cycle for capital works:\n1. **Initiation:** Divisions and Zonal HQs prepare proposals for new lines, doubling, traffic facilities, passenger amenities.\n2. **Financial Scrutiny:** Associate Finance vets the technical and financial justification, ROR calculations, and operational necessity.\n3. **Zonal Works Programme (ZWP):** Approved by GM and sent to Railway Board.\n4. **Pink Book:** The final Parliament-approved list of capital works included in the Union Budget, containing project cost, expenditure up to last year, current year budget outlay, and balance funds required.\n- **Categories of Works:**\n  - *Pink Book Works:* Works costing above Rs. 2.5 Crore (sanctioned by Railway Board / Parliament).\n  - *LAW Book Works (List of Approved Works):* Works costing between Rs. 50 Lakhs and Rs. 2.5 Crore (sanctioned by GM).\n  - *Umbrella Works:* Large generic sanctions under which individual sub-works are approved by Zonal GMs.\n\n### 2. Financial Justification & Rate of Return (ROR)\nEvery commercial capital investment proposal must prove its financial viability:\n- **Discounted Cash Flow (DCF) Method:**\n  Takes into account the time value of money. Calculates the Internal Rate of Return (IRR) where Net Present Value (NPV) of future net earnings equals capital cost:\n  $$\\sum_{t=0}^{n} \\frac{C_t}{(1 + r)^t} = 0$$\n- **Benchmark ROR:** Minimum **10%** (previously 14%). Works failing to yield 10% cannot be sanctioned as remunerative works (must be justified on safety, operational, or strategic grounds).\n\n### 3. Types of Engineering Estimates (IRFC Vol. I Chapter V)\n| Estimate Type | Trigger / Purpose | Key Rules & Limits |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Abstract Estimate (Para 510)** | Prepared to obtain preliminary administrative approval and budget inclusion | Rough approximate cost based on per-km or per-sqm rates |\n| **Detailed Estimate (Para 513)** | Prepared for technical sanction after work is included in Pink Book | Exact quantities, rates, site drawings, and detailed schedule |\n| **Supplementary Estimate (Para 514)** | Prepared for items not originally anticipated or included in original estimate | Debited to the same project; requires financial concurrence |\n| **Revised Estimate (Para 515)** | Prepared when project cost exceeds sanctioned estimate by **more than 10%** or material deviation | Sanction of original sanctioning authority required |\n| **Completion Report (Para 517)** | Prepared within **6 months** of completion of the work | Compares sanctioned vs actual outlay, liquidates liabilities |\n\n### 4. Reappropriation of Funds\n- Transfer of funds from one sanctioned work or budget sub-head to another having savings.\n- **Powers & Restrictions:**\n  - Cannot reappropriate from Voted to Charged or vice versa.\n  - Cannot reappropriate from Capital to Revenue.\n  - Cannot reappropriate funds allotted for Pink Book works to unapproved works.\n  - General Managers have powers to reappropriate within the same Plan Head between works within their sanctioning power.\n",
