    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. IPAS (Integrated Payroll & Accounting System)\nDeveloped by CRIS, IPAS has unified the accounting architecture of Indian Railways into a single centralized cloud platform:\n- **Key Modules in IPAS:**\n  1. **Payroll Module:** Calculates pay, allowances, recoveries, and direct credit to bank accounts.\n  2. **Internal Check / Passing Module:** Electronic passing of contractor bills, stores bills, contingent vouchers.\n  3. **Books & Budget Module:** General Books, Compilation of Monthly Accounts, Appropriation Accounts, Exchequer Control.\n  4. **Provident Fund Module:** Automated interest calculation, non-refundable withdrawals, loan advances.\n  5. **Pension & Settlement Module:** Gratuity, commutation, monthly pension compilation (integrated with ARPAN).\n  6. **GST Module:** Consolidation of input tax credit (ITC) and filing of monthly GSTR-1, GSTR-3B, and GSTR-7 returns.\n\n### 2. IREPS (Indian Railways E-Procurement System)\n- India's largest government procurement portal by transaction volume.\n- Zero manual touchpoints for:\n  - Goods procurement (IRS tenders).\n  - Works & Services tenders (GCC 2022).\n  - Electronic Auction of scrap rolling stock, rails, and obsolete machinery.\n  - Electronic Reverse Auction (e-RA).\n\n### 3. User Depot Module (UDM)\n- Extended the reach of electronic material management down to the grassroots level:\n  - Covers SSE (Permanent Way), SSE (Signal), SSE (C&W), Electrical Foreman, Station Master imprests.\n  - Ensures complete visibility of consumed materials, eliminating phantom requisitions and excessive hoarding.\n  - Automatically raises digital indents to stores depots when stock dips below re-order level (ROL).\n\n### 4. TAMS (Traffic Accounts Management System)\n- Replaces manual audit of millions of passenger tickets and freight receipts.\n- Direct electronic interface with CRIS PRS, UTS, and FOIS.\n- Performs automated apportionment of revenue and generates error sheets electronically.\n",
