    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. GST Architecture in Indian Railways\nSince 01.07.2017, Indian Railways operates as a registered taxable entity:\n- **GSTIN Structure (15 Digits):**\n  - E.g., `07AAAGM0289C1Z4` (07 = State Code, AAAGM0289C = Ministry of Railways PAN, 1 = Entity number, Z = Default alphabet, 4 = Check code).\n  - Railways holds separate GST registrations in **all 36 States and Union Territories**.\n- **Taxation of Railway Revenue:**\n  - *Passenger Fares:* Non-AC sleeper and unreserved travel are **exempt** from GST. AC classes (AC 1, AC 2, AC 3, CC, Executive, Vande Bharat) are taxed at **5%** (with ITC on input services).\n  - *Freight Services:* Taxed at **5%** (input tax credit on input services admissible).\n  - *Sundry Services:* Catering, stall licenses, parking lots, cloakrooms, commercial advertisements taxed at **18%**.\n- **TDS under GST (Section 51 of CGST Act):**\n  - Deducted at **2%** (1% CGST + 1% SGST or 2% IGST) from payments made to suppliers of taxable goods or services where total contract value exceeds **Rs. 2,50,000**.\n  - Deposited by the 10th of the following month via GSTR-7 return, issuing Form GSTR-7A certificate to the vendor.\n\n### 2. Income Tax Deductions (TDS) under Income Tax Act, 1961\n1. **Section 192 (Salaries):**\n   - Monthly tax deducted from employee salaries based on average rate of income tax.\n   - Option between **New Tax Regime** (default under Section 115BAC with reduced slab rates and standard deduction of Rs. 75,000) and **Old Tax Regime** (with deductions under 80C, 80D, HRA).\n   - Annual certificate issued in **Form 16**.\n2. **Section 194C (Payments to Contractors):**\n   - Deducted at **1%** if payee is an Individual or HUF.\n   - Deducted at **2%** if payee is a Company, Firm, or other entity.\n   - Threshold: Single bill > Rs. 30,000 or aggregate annual payment > Rs. 1,00,000.\n3. **Section 194J (Fees for Professional or Technical Services):**\n   - Deducted at **2%** for technical services / call center operators.\n   - Deducted at **10%** for professional services (advocate legal fees, medical consultants).\n   - Threshold: Rs. 30,000 per financial year.\n",
