    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Execution Runtimes: JVM vs CLR vs Native Compilation\n```\n [ C / C++ Source ] \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba Compiler \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Native Machine Code (.exe / .so) ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba Hardware Execution\n\n [ Java Source ]    \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba javac    \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Java Bytecode (.class) ]\n                                                        \u2502\n                                                        \u25bc\n                                       \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n                                       \u2502 Java Virtual Machine (JVM)       \u2502\n                                       \u2502 - ClassLoader                    \u2502\n                                       \u2502 - HotSpot JIT (Tiered C1/C2)     \u2502\n                                       \u2502 - Garbage Collector (G1 / ZGC)   \u2502\n                                       \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n\n [ C# Source ]       \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba csc      \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Common Intermediate Language (CIL) ]\n                                                        \u2502\n                                                        \u25bc\n                                       \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n                                       \u2502 Common Language Runtime (CLR)    \u2502\n                                       \u2502 - Virtual Execution System (VES) \u2502\n                                       \u2502 - RyuJIT Compiler                \u2502\n                                       \u2502 - Generational GC (Gen 0, 1, 2)  \u2502\n                                       \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n### 2. Production Code Snippets: Memory & Architecture\n\n#### A. C Language: Pointers and Dynamic Memory Allocation\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    int train_no;\n    char train_name[50];\n    int available_berths;\n} TrainRecord;\n\nint main(void) {\n    // Allocate array of 10 TrainRecord structures on the Heap\n    TrainRecord *fleet = (TrainRecord *)malloc(10 * sizeof(TrainRecord));\n    if (fleet == NULL) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Fatal: Out of Memory!\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    fleet[0].train_no = 12951;\n    strncpy(fleet[0].train_name, \"Mumbai Rajdhani Express\", sizeof(fleet[0].train_name) - 1);\n    fleet[0].available_berths = 120;\n\n    printf(\"Train %d (%s) - Berths: %d\\n\", \n           fleet[0].train_no, fleet[0].train_name, fleet[0].available_berths);\n\n    // Critical: Free dynamically allocated heap memory to avoid memory leak\n    free(fleet);\n    fleet = NULL; // Prevent dangling pointer\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n#### B. Java: Enterprise Service with Robust Concurrency\n```java\npackage in.gov.indianrailways.edp;\n\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\npublic class BerthAllocationService {\n    // Thread-safe concurrent map tracking berth availability per coach class\n    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, AtomicInteger> berthInventory = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n    public BerthAllocationService() {\n        berthInventory.put(\"3A\", new AtomicInteger(64));\n        berthInventory.put(\"2A\", new AtomicInteger(48));\n        berthInventory.put(\"1A\", new AtomicInteger(18));\n    }\n\n    public boolean reserveBerth(String coachClass) {\n        AtomicInteger count = berthInventory.get(coachClass);\n        if (count == null) return false;\n\n        // Atomic lock-free decrement\n        int remaining = count.updateAndGet(current -> (current > 0) ? current - 1 : 0);\n        return remaining >= 0;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### C. COBOL: Complete Standard Production Batch Program\n```cobol\n       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.\n       PROGRAM-ID. RAILPAY.\n       AUTHOR. INDIAN-RAILWAYS-EDP.\n      *-----------------------------------------------------------------\n      * BATCH PAYROLL ACCRUAL PROCESSOR\n      *-----------------------------------------------------------------\n       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.\n       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.\n       FILE-CONTROL.\n           SELECT EMP-IN-FILE ASSIGN TO \"EMPMAST.DAT\"\n               ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL\n               FILE STATUS IS WS-FILE-STATUS.\n           SELECT PAY-OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO \"PAYROLL.DAT\"\n               ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.\n\n       DATA DIVISION.\n       FILE SECTION.\n       FD  EMP-IN-FILE.\n       01  EMP-RECORD.\n           05  EMP-ID          PIC 9(08).\n           05  EMP-NAME        PIC X(25).\n           05  EMP-BASIC-PAY   PIC 9(07)V99.\n           05  EMP-DA-RATE     PIC 9(03)V99.\n\n       FD  PAY-OUT-FILE.\n       01  PAY-RECORD.\n           05  PR-EMP-ID       PIC 9(08).\n           05  PR-EMP-NAME     PIC X(25).\n           05  PR-GROSS-PAY    PIC 9(08)V99.\n\n       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.\n       01  WS-FILE-STATUS      PIC X(02) VALUE \"00\".\n       01  WS-EOF-SWITCH       PIC X(01) VALUE \"N\".\n           88 END-OF-FILE                VALUE \"Y\".\n       01  WS-TOTAL-RECORDS    PIC 9(06) VALUE ZERO.\n       01  WS-CALC-DA          PIC 9(07)V99 VALUE ZERO.\n\n       PROCEDURE DIVISION.\n       0000-MAIN-LOGIC.\n           OPEN INPUT  EMP-IN-FILE\n                OUTPUT PAY-OUT-FILE.\n           \n           PERFORM 1000-PROCESS-RECORD UNTIL END-OF-FILE.\n           \n           CLOSE EMP-IN-FILE\n                 PAY-OUT-FILE.\n           DISPLAY \"TOTAL EMPLOYEES PROCESSED: \" WS-TOTAL-RECORDS.\n           STOP RUN.\n\n       1000-PROCESS-RECORD.\n           READ EMP-IN-FILE\n               AT END\n                   SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE\n               NOT AT END\n                   ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-RECORDS\n                   MOVE EMP-ID TO PR-EMP-ID\n                   MOVE EMP-NAME TO PR-EMP-NAME\n                   COMPUTE WS-CALC-DA = EMP-BASIC-PAY * (EMP-DA-RATE / 100)\n                   COMPUTE PR-GROSS-PAY = EMP-BASIC-PAY + WS-CALC-DA\n                   WRITE PAY-RECORD\n           END-READ.\n```\n",
