    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Solid Modeling: CSG vs B-Rep Comparison\n```\n  CONSTRUCTIVE SOLID GEOMETRY (CSG)              BOUNDARY REPRESENTATION (B-Rep)\n            [ Solid Cylinder ]                               [ Face F1 ]\n                  \u2502                                         /     |            (Difference Operator -)                      [ Edge E1 ] [ Edge E2 ] [ Edge E3 ]\n                  \u25bc                                        \\      |      /\n            [ Solid Block ]                                  [ Vertex V1 ]\n   * Defined as a binary tree of boolean          * Defined topologically by explicit\n     combinations of geometric primitives.          boundaries: Vertices, Edges, and Faces.\n```\n\n### 2. CNC G-Code & M-Code Reference Table\n| Code | Type | Meaning & Function | Syntax / Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **G00** | Modal Motion | Rapid traverse positioning (non-cutting motion at maximum machine speed) | `G00 X50.0 Y100.0` |\n| **G01** | Modal Motion | Linear interpolation cutting motion at programmed feed rate ($F$) | `G01 X150.0 Y100.0 F250` |\n| **G02** | Modal Motion | Circular interpolation cutting motion in Clockwise (CW) direction | `G02 X200.0 Y50.0 R50.0 F180` |\n| **G03** | Modal Motion | Circular interpolation cutting motion in Counter-Clockwise (CCW) direction | `G03 X100.0 Y150.0 R50.0 F180` |\n| **G90** | Modal Mode | Absolute programming coordinate system (referenced from workpiece zero) | `G90` |\n| **G91** | Modal Mode | Incremental programming coordinate system (referenced from current tool position) | `G91` |\n| **M03** | Spindle | Start spindle rotation Clockwise (CW) at speed $S$ | `M03 S1500` |\n| **M05** | Spindle | Spindle stop | `M05` |\n| **M08** | Coolant | Flood coolant pump ON | `M08` |\n| **M09** | Coolant | Flood coolant pump OFF | `M09` |\n| **M30** | Program | End of CNC program and reset tool to home position | `M30` |\n\n### 3. Complete CNC Part Program for Rail Axle Journal Machining\n```gcode\n%\nO1001 (RAILWAY AXLE JOURNAL FINISH TURNING)\nG21          (Metric programming in millimeters)\nG90          (Absolute programming mode)\nG96 S180 M03 (Constant surface speed 180 m/min, spindle CW)\nG00 X120.0 Z5.0 (Rapid positioning to safety clearance point)\nM08          (Coolant ON)\nG01 Z0.0 F0.5   (Touch axle face)\nG01 X130.0 Z-50.0 F0.25 (Linear finish cut along journal bearing seat)\nG02 X150.0 Z-60.0 R10.0 F0.2 (Circular fillet radius cut R10)\nG01 Z-120.0  (Turn remaining journal collar)\nG00 X200.0 Z50.0 (Retract tool rapidly)\nM09          (Coolant OFF)\nM05          (Spindle STOP)\nM30          (End of program and rewind)\n%\n```\n",
