    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. UIDAI Aadhaar Authentication Architecture\n```\n [ Mobile / Web App ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ RD Service Biometric Device ]\n          \u2502                         \u2502\n          \u2502                   (Captures & Encrypts PID Block with UIDAI Public Key)\n          \u25bc                         \u2502\n [ Sub-AUA / AUA (CRIS) ] \u25c4\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n          \u2502\n          \u2502 Encapsulates into signed XML Request over TLS 1.3\n          \u25bc\n [ ASA (Authentication Service Agency) ]\n          \u2502\n          \u2502 Dedicated leased line / MPLS\n          \u25bc\n [ UIDAI Central Identities Data Repository (CIDR) ]\n          \u2502\n          \u251c\u2500\u2500\u25ba Match PID against 1.4+ Billion Biometric Templates\n          \u25bc\n Returns Signed Response: <AuthRes code=\"y/n\" err=\"\" ts=\"\" txn=\"\" />\n```\n\n### 2. SOAP vs RESTful API Architectural Comparison\n| Parameter | SOAP (Simple Object Access Protocol) | REST (Representational State Transfer) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Protocol Nature** | Formal protocol with strict messaging rules | Architectural style with flexible implementation |\n| **Payload Format** | Strictly XML | Multiformat: JSON (primary), XML, YAML, Protocol Buffers |\n| **Contract / Schema** | WSDL (Web Services Description Language) | OpenAPI Specification (OAS 3.0 / Swagger) |\n| **Transport Protocol**| HTTP, SMTP, TCP, JMS | Exclusively HTTP / HTTPS |\n| **State Management**  | Can be stateful or stateless | Strictly stateless (every request carries full context) |\n| **Performance**       | Slower due to XML parsing and verbose envelopes| Highly performant, lightweight JSON serialization |\n| **Enterprise Use**    | Legacy banking, telecommunications backbones | Modern web apps, mobile apps, microservices, RailMadad |\n",
