    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. XML Parsing: DOM vs SAX Parser Comparison\n| Feature | Document Object Model (DOM) | Simple API for XML (SAX) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Mechanism** | Tree-based in-memory parser | Event-driven streaming parser |\n| **Memory Footprint**| High ($O(N)$ - loads entire document into RAM) | Minimal ($O(1)$ - processes line by line) |\n| **Traversal** | Bidirectional, random access, XPath queries | Forward-only, sequential single-pass |\n| **Modification** | Can create, modify, delete, and re-serialize nodes | Read-only; cannot alter the document in place |\n| **Speed** | Slower for massive files (>100 MB) | Extremely fast for large stream processing |\n| **Railway Use** | Configuration files, small SOAP messages | Streaming multi-gigabyte freight log XML feeds |\n\n### 2. Production Code Snippets: XML & PHP\n\n#### A. Valid XML Document with Embedded XSD Schema\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<train_schedule xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\">\n    <train train_number=\"12952\">\n        <name>Mumbai - New Delhi Rajdhani Express</name>\n        <origin>MMCT</origin>\n        <destination>NDLS</destination>\n        <distance_km>1384</distance_km>\n        <active_days>Daily</active_days>\n    </train>\n</train_schedule>\n```\n\n#### B. Production PHP 8.x Script: Secure PDO Database Query\n```php\n<?php\n// Production PHP 8.x PDO script with Prepared Statements (SQL Injection Safe)\ndeclare(strict_types=1);\n\n$dsn = \"pgsql:host=localhost;port=5432;dbname=railway_edp;\";\n$username = \"edp_admin\";\n$password = getenv(\"DB_PASSWORD\"); // Secure environment variable lookup\n\n$options = [\n    PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE            => PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION,\n    PDO::ATTR_DEFAULT_FETCH_MODE => PDO::FETCH_ASSOC,\n    PDO::ATTR_EMULATE_PREPARES   => false, // Enforce native prepared statements\n];\n\ntry {\n    $pdo = new PDO($dsn, $username, $password, $options);\n    \n    $pnrInput = filter_input(INPUT_POST, 'pnr_no', FILTER_SANITIZE_SPECIAL_CHARS);\n    \n    // Parameterized prepared query prevents SQL injection\n    $stmt = $pdo->prepare(\"SELECT pnr_no, train_no, passenger_name, berth_status \n                           FROM passenger_reservations \n                           WHERE pnr_no = :pnr\");\n    $stmt->execute(['pnr' => $pnrInput]);\n    \n    $passenger = $stmt->fetch();\n    \n    if ($passenger) {\n        echo json_encode(['status' => 'SUCCESS', 'data' => $passenger]);\n    } else {\n        http_response_code(404);\n        echo json_encode(['status' => 'NOT_FOUND', 'message' => 'PNR record does not exist.']);\n    }\n} catch (PDOException $e) {\n    error_log(\"Database Error: \" . $e->getMessage());\n    http_response_code(500);\n    echo json_encode(['status' => 'ERROR', 'message' => 'Internal server error.']);\n}\n```\n",
